{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nAt current origin/main commit 0f5dbc88b with Mypy 2.3.0, the base command mypy src/rebar exits 0. Adding strict_equality also exits 0. Adding no_implicit_optional exposes the same redundant-cast diagnostic described below and no optionality diagnostic. The exact redundant-cast command exits 1 with the redundant-cast diagnostics live on the current `origin/main` tip; at plan authoring that was a single diagnostic, src/rebar/llm/workflow/editor.py:515: error: Redundant cast to \"int\" [redundant-cast] (editor.py has two cast() calls at lines 514-515; the str cast at line 514 was not diagnosed). Any additional redundant-cast site surfaced live on current `origin/main` is remediated too. The exact warn_unused_ignores command reports the live set of diagnostics for the current `origin/main` tip (24 across 20 source files at plan authoring, commit 0f5dbc88b; treat that as a dated observation, not the contract). Because unused-ignore results can change with Mypy, Python, dependency stubs, and optional extras, cleanup must be performed only in the pinned, fully provisioned CI environment.\n\n## Approach\n1. Depend on the approved dependency-freezing work to pin the canonical Mypy version and provision all project extras used by CI.\n2. Add a failing ratchet test that requires no_implicit_optional, strict_equality, warn_redundant_casts, and warn_unused_ignores while explicitly preserving the deferral of disallow_any_generics and disallow_untyped_defs.\n3. Capture the standalone diagnostic output in the canonical environment.\n4. Remove the int cast at editor.py:515 after the command above proves it redundant. Retain the adjacent str cast unless Mypy independently diagnoses it.\n5. Inspect the suppressed error and relevant optional-dependency environment for each live unused-ignore diagnostic reported against current `origin/main`. Remove an ignore only when the canonical fully provisioned environment proves it stale; otherwise preserve it and narrow or document configuration.\n6. Enable the four approved global settings and run the exact verification commands below.\n\nRejected: enabling disallow_any_generics or disallow_untyped_defs. Rejected: deleting ignores solely from output produced by an incompletely provisioned environment.\n\n## Scope\nConfiguration and ratchet:\n- pyproject.toml\n- tests/unit/test_mypy_ratchet.py\n\nRedundant-cast inspection:\n- src/rebar/llm/workflow/editor.py:514-515\n\nThe warn_unused_ignores diagnostics observed at plan authoring (commit 0f5dbc88b, dated reference only — the live set against current `origin/main` is authoritative):\n- src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/outbound_comments.py:60\n- src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/inbound_fields.py:42\n- src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/inbound_differ.py:68\n- src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/differ.py:37,77\n- src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/apply_base.py:39\n- src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/reconcile_check.py:37\n- src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/binding_store.py:228\n- src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/reconcile.py:36\n- src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/_ref_lock.py:86\n- src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/reconcile_helpers.py:44\n- src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/invariants.py:213\n- src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira/acli.py:468\n- src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/run_differs.py:46\n- src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/rebar_id_audit.py:48\n- src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/_advisory_lock.py:51\n- src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira/outbound_fields.py:67\n- src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/inbound_translate.py:151,311\n- src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/__main__.py:70,102\n- src/rebar/llm/workflow/schema.py:86,100\n- src/rebar/mcp_server.py:644\n\nLine numbers identify the observed Mypy 2.3.0 baseline at commit 0f5dbc88b. Newly surfaced diagnostics are recorded as discovered work rather than silently expanding this story.\n\n## Testing / Verification\n- Configuration: pytest -q tests/unit/test_mypy_ratchet.py\n- Standalone Mypy: mypy src/rebar --warn-redundant-casts\n- Standalone Mypy: mypy src/rebar --warn-unused-ignores\n- Canonical type gate: make typecheck\n- Behavior-adjacent tests: pytest -q tests/unit/workflow/test_editor.py tests/unit/workflow/test_schema.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_cli.py tests/unit/rebar_reconciler tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp.py\n- Default tier: pytest -m \"not integration and not external\" -q\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] tests/unit/test_mypy_ratchet.py asserts no_implicit_optional, strict_equality, warn_redundant_casts, and warn_unused_ignores are enabled globally.\n- [ ] [operator-attested] Before remediation, the ticket contains a comment naming the pinned Mypy version, the current `origin/main` commit, the redundant-cast command, its exit code, and each redundant-cast diagnostic observed live against current `origin/main`.\n- [ ] mypy src/rebar --warn-redundant-casts exits 0 after remediation.\n- [ ] mypy src/rebar --warn-unused-ignores exits 0 after remediation.\n- [ ] make typecheck exits 0.\n- [ ] [operator-attested] A ticket comment maps each live warn_unused_ignores diagnostic (measured against current `origin/main`) to removed, preserved-and-narrowed, or preserved-and-documented.\n- [ ] The editor diff removes the diagnosed int cast and retains the adjacent str cast unless a new recorded Mypy diagnostic proves it redundant.\n- [ ] tests/unit/test_mypy_ratchet.py asserts disallow_any_generics and disallow_untyped_defs are not enabled globally.\n- [ ] pytest -q tests/unit/workflow/test_editor.py tests/unit/workflow/test_schema.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_cli.py tests/unit/rebar_reconciler tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp.py exits 0.\n- [ ] pytest -m \"not integration and not external\" -q exits 0.\n\n<!-- green-on-origin-main AC -->\n- [ ] After `git fetch origin`, `make typecheck` exits 0 against the **current** `origin/main` with no_implicit_optional, strict_equality, warn_redundant_casts, and warn_unused_ignores enabled; any pre-existing diagnostic in these families on current `origin/main` (including drift-introduced since the measured commit) is resolved before the flags are landed.\n"}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785954222247904001,"uuid":"b2c59172-7fcc-43dd-933e-3a528ed0b2cb"}